# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your free Twelve Data API key.
# Get one at: https://twelvedata.com/pricing  (Basic / free plan)
TWELVE_DATA_API_KEY=TWELVE_DATA_API_KEY

# REQUIRED: Turso (libSQL) database. All state — portfolios, company names, the
# profile cache, the screener snapshot and the visitor log — lives here. The app
# no longer writes JSON files, because a serverless filesystem (Vercel) discards
# them. Create a database at https://turso.tech, then copy its URL and a token.
# These same two values must also be set in the Vercel project's env vars.
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db-your-org.turso.io
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-auth-token

# Optional but strongly recommended once public: require an invite code to create
# an account. Without it, anyone who finds the URL can register themselves. Share
# the code only with people you want to let in. When unset, sign-up is open.
# SIGNUP_CODE=some-shared-phrase

# Optional: change the port the server listens on (default 3000)
# PORT=3000

# Optional (for publishing): make the app READ-ONLY for the public. When set, the
# public sees a cached snapshot and can only sort / collapse groups / export; adding
# or removing tickers, Refresh, Refresh All and backtests require logging in with
# this password (a "🔒 Admin login" button appears). When UNSET (the default), the
# app is fully open — every action is available with no login (local development).
# Pick a strong value before deploying to a public URL.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-to-something-strong

# Optional: populate the fundamental columns (market cap, forward P/E, PEG, quarterly
# earnings growth). These come from the /statistics endpoint, which requires a Twelve
# Data PRO plan or higher. On lower tiers it 403s for real tickers, so it's OFF by
# default. Enable only after upgrading to Pro+:
# ENABLE_FUNDAMENTALS=true
#
# (Sector, via /profile, works on standard paid plans and is always fetched.)

# Optional: populate the Analyst columns (consensus + average price target). These use
# /recommendations and /price_target, which require a Twelve Data ULTRA plan or higher
# (they 403 on Pro for real tickers). OFF by default; enable only on Ultra+:
# ENABLE_ANALYST=true

# Optional: the built-in assistant at /chat. Without this key the page loads but
# every question returns "not configured". Get one at https://console.anthropic.com.
# The whole screener snapshot (~17,500 tokens for 69 stocks) is sent as the system
# prompt and cached, so after the first question you pay only for the question and
# the answer. Answers include the model's reasoning, which is billed as output.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Optional: which model answers (default claude-sonnet-5). The work is numeric
# reasoning over dozens of rows, which is where smaller models get sloppy.
# CHAT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#
# Optional: questions per user per UTC day. The first applies to the owner, the
# second to everyone else. Counted per account, so a shared login shares the
# allowance rather than multiplying it.
# CHAT_DAILY_LIMIT=60
# CHAT_DAILY_LIMIT_MEMBER=3

# Optional: password-reset and welcome emails, via Resend (https://resend.com).
# All three are required together — without them the "forgot password" endpoint
# still replies normally but sends nothing, so it never reveals the difference.
# Send from a subdomain (mail.yourdomain.com) so a reputation problem cannot
# reach the domain the site itself is served from, and add a DMARC record at the
# root: v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:you@example.com
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# MAIL_FROM=Ticker Lab <no-reply@mail.example.com>
# APP_URL=https://www.example.com
#
# Optional: where replies go. Nothing receives mail at the sending address, so
# without this a reply vanishes silently.
# MAIL_REPLY_TO=you@example.com
#
# Optional: where the /contact form delivers. Falls back to the owner account's
# own email, so the form works even if this is never set.
# CONTACT_TO=you@example.com
# CONTACT_DAILY_LIMIT=10
